[
  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013841",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-121424",
      "knowledge_point_id": "ee633017-5c17-575f-bdab-5f12b7319355",
      "knowledge_point": "Expressing the Area Between Two Curves as an Integral Given the Limits of Integration",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013841/assets/a928b14cfe88f9aaf7b8cf5288a18f3e81e163ea65fd3a48653fcba630c11386.png)\n\nWhich integral gives the area of the finite region bounded by $y=8{x}^{2}-5$ and $y=1-2x,$ shown above?\n\n*(Note: Figure not drawn to scale)*",
      "worked_solution": "The diagram shows that the intersection points between the two graphs occur when $x=-1$ and $x=\\frac{3}{4}.$ So these will be our limits of integration.\n\nTo determine which is the lower function and which is the upper, let's draw our vertical arrow.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013841/assets/226ade4a3b546484ba2e9ce5f266391fb51e9fe4b62e2e78d12200ac54ecea9a.png)\n\nThe vertical line \n\n- *enters* the region through the lower function $y=8{x}^{2}-5,$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the upper function $y=1-2x.$\n\nTherefore, the integral that gives our area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3/4}[\\,(\\text{upper function})-(\\text{lower function})\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3/4}[\\,(1-2x)-(8{x}^{2}-5)\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3/4}(-8{x}^{2}-2x+6)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{-1/3}^{3/4}(-{x}^{2}-2x+6)\\,\\text{d}x",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{1}^{3/4}(-8{x}^{2}+x+5)\\,\\text{d}x",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{-1/4}^{3/4}(-8{x}^{2}-2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{-1}^{3/4}(8{x}^{2}-x-4)\\,\\text{d}x",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{-1}^{3/4}(-8{x}^{2}-2x+6)\\,\\text{d}x",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "provenance": {
