  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013841",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-3121",
      "knowledge_point_id": "ee633017-5c17-575f-bdab-5f12b7319355",
      "knowledge_point": "Expressing the Area Between Two Curves as an Integral Given the Limits of Integration",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013841/assets/9a87ae2b230e66b685051ee7d13987f5f68690a07a67ade9e7af0eb870f6224f.png)\n\nWhich integral gives the area of the finite region bounded by $y=2{x}^{2}$ and $y=x+1,$ as shown above?\n\n*(Note: Figure not drawn to scale)*",
      "worked_solution": "The diagram shows that the intersection points between the two graphs occur when $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $x=1.$ So these will be our limits of integration.\n\nTo determine which is the lower function and which is the upper, let's draw our vertical arrow.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013841/assets/e77170aac6d81b1cfd0e93804b0c59802f28089d24aeaff065da04cabc44c172.png)\n\nThe vertical line \n\n- *enters* the region through the lower function $y=2{x}^{2},$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the upper function $y=x+1.$\n\nTherefore, the integral that gives our area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1}[\\,(\\text{upper function})-(\\text{lower function})\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1}[\\,(x+1)-(2{x}^{2})\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1}(x+1-2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1}(2{x}^{2}+x-1)\\,\\text{d}x",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1}(2{x}^{2}-x-1)\\,\\text{d}x",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1}(x+1-2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1}(x-1-2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1}(x-1+2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "provenance": {
