  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013841",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-3146",
      "knowledge_point_id": "8fa1bebf-4af0-5a5c-962c-8a88f8392776",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Area Between Two Curves Expressed as Functions of X",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013841/assets/c61d9140e5b8e57c8f75b532c6e26e22faa073e6631984a8f6a7b6f4280882e3.png)\n\nFind the area of the finite region enclosed between $y={x}^{2}+4x$ and $y=x,$ shown above.\n\n*(Note: Figure not drawn to scale)*",
      "worked_solution": "First, we want to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we equate the two functions and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4x & =x \\\\ {x}^{2}+3x & =0 \\\\ x(x+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $x=-3$ to $x=0.$\n\nTo determine which is the lower function and which is the upper, we draw our vertical arrow.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013841/assets/6b2232d5a2853b22c731c317b365822e371f3d419bfcb3e528a07f211a372553.png)\n\nThe vertical line \n\n- *enters* the region through the lower function $y={x}^{2}+4x,$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the upper function $y=x.$\n\nTherefore, the integral that gives our area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}[\\,(\\text{upper function})-(\\text{lower function})\\,]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}[\\,(x)-({x}^{2}+4x)\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}(-{x}^{2}-3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{-3}^{0} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {0}^{2}]-[-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-3)^{3}-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (-3)^{2}] \\\\  & =(0)-(9-\\frac{27}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\frac{9}{2}",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
